\subsection{\textbf{Unlasting} Performs Well on OOD Drug Perturbation and Double Gene Perturbation}
To further validate the effectiveness of \textbf{Unlasting}, we evaluate its performance on double gene knockouts using the Norman dataset (\cite{norman}) and on out-of-distribution (OOD) drugs, as described in Section~\ref{split}. Double gene knockouts involve complex gene–gene interactions, and experimental results show that our model effectively captures these interactions. To predict the effects of double gene perturbations, we use all observed samples under single gene perturbations and unperturbed conditions as the training set. OOD drugs, which are not seen during training, primarily target epigenetic regulation, tyrosine kinase signaling, and cell cycle regulation \cite{ood}. These drugs are representative of key biological processes and are often distinct from the drug in the training set. Our model demonstrates superior performance, suggesting that it better captures the effects of unseen molecules on cellular behavior.

