\begin{abstract}
In this paper we consider nonzero harmonic functions vanishing on certain subvarieties of $\mathbb R^n$. Among other things, we give a positive solution to the Problem 151 from the Scottish Book posed by R. Wavre in 1936. In more detail, we construct a nonzero harmonic function in the whole space that vanishes on the edges of the unit cube. Moreover, using harmonic morphsims we construct  certain new nontrivial families of harmonic polynomials that vanish at the same set in the unit ball in $\mathbb R^n$ for all $n\geq 4$. This extends results of Logunov and Malinnikova from~\cite{logunov2015ratios}. We also present some (presumably) new results on  harmonic functions in the space whose nodal sets are unions of (affine) subspaces.
