$M^{(4)}_4 = \frac{1}{2} \left[\begin{array}{cccc}
1 & -i & -1 & -i\\
1 & -i & 1 & i\\
1 & i & -1 & i\\
1 & i & 1 & -i\\
\end{array}\right]$.

There is only a pair of real MUBs in this case. Now the question is can we extend this, and the answer is affirmative with the following example with 3 real MUBs. 

$M'_{1} =
        \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\begin{bmatrix} 
