  \subsection{Test Case 3: Two-Dimensional Layered Medium}
  In this test case, we showcase the ability of \maggnn to handle physical domains associated with multiple physical quantities.
  As explained in Section~\ref{sec:sagehetero}, SAGE-Heterogeneous can only handle two distinct physical parts at most. If we consider a mesh with more than two physical parameters, the only option is to use the \emph{segregated} mode. We demonstrate this by agglomerating a mesh of a layered medium, including seven different physical parameters, using the SAGE-Base model. The mesh represens an idealized bidimensional Earth's cross-section $\Omega = (0, 38.4) \text{km} \times (0, 10) \text{km}$ used for the simulation of seismic wave propagation \cite{antonietti2021PolyDGgeophysicalsimulations}. The results are reported in Figure~\ref{fig:mesh_emilia}.

